A repo at your level sent you something, or answered you. Read `docs/InOutBox/inbox/<peer>/` and `pact/<peer>/` at session start, with the announcement sweep. Starting an exchange → `sdh-peer-channel-send`; a REQ arrived → `sdh-cross-repo-req-answer` (there you owe an answer).

The app delivers: it mirrors the peer's outbox into your `inbox/` and merges `pact/`. Never write into `inbox/`, never copy across repos. The author's copy is the truth — disagree in your own file, never by editing theirs.

## What you owe

| Arrived | You owe |
|---|---|
| `PACT-NNN.md` | an answer: `PACT-NNN_<slug>.ack.md` in your `pact/<peer>/` — the only kind that blocks |
| `HANDOFF-NNN.md` | remove the handed-over area from your `docs/todo.md` |
| `NOTE-NNN.md` | check whether it applies; if so, file your own task |
| `.ack.md` on your proposal | act on the verdict, then close |

## Ack

First line — the status, then the reasoning:
- `agreed`;
- `agreed-with-limits` — list each limit;
- `declined` — a legitimate answer; say why, and propose an alternative as a new pact of your own;
- `clarification-needed` — a question back; the pact stays open.

**Two rounds of clarification without `agreed` or `declined` → mark the pact escalated and give the decision to the owner.** No third round.

## Closing

- PACT → the initiator drops `.impl.md`; HANDOFF / NOTE → the sender drops `.done.md`. The app removes the files on both sides. As a recipient you delete nothing.
- Log every incoming exchange in your own `docs/InOutBox/registry.md` with direction `in` — the counter is `max` over the whole file.
- Whoever drops the marker fills `closed`, final status and where the result went in the same pass. Missing registry → create it.

## Never

- Agree with a peer about what the level above owns: each sends its own REQ up; the pact may record who sends it.
- Treat the channel as a task list: an accepted pact becomes a task in your `docs/todo.md`.
